;;
;; panic-attack assail user-classification registry (DEED praxis form).
;; Read first by panic-attack (src/assail/classifications.rs, DEED_PATH);
;; when this file exists the legacy audits/assail-classifications.a2ml is
;; never read. Form: see that module's docs. Each (classification ...)
;; suppresses the finding at :file for :category, so every entry must name
;; a real audit, not boilerplate.
;;
;; This registry is deliberately EMPTY. It replaces the retired
;; audits/assail-classifications.a2ml, whose 14 entries used a `- suppression:`
;; YAML dialect that panic-attack's legacy reader never parsed, so none of
;; them ever suppressed anything. They all carried the same generic text
;; ("Automated estate triage: reviewed as safe ..."), not an audit of the
;; file. They are kept below as UNREVIEWED CANDIDATES, NOT ACTIVE. To activate
;; one, audit the finding at source and add a (classification ...) clause
;; with a specific :audit and :rationale.
;;
;;   CommandInjection     config/validate.sh
;;   CommandInjection     tests/ai-isolation/network-tests/container_escape_test.sh
;;   CommandInjection     scripts/install/install.sh
;;   DynamicCodeExecution examples/demos/web-ui/app.js
;;   HardcodedSecret      monitoring/healthchecks/healthcheck.sh
;;   HardcodedSecret      monitoring/scripts/backup_dashboards.sh
;;   HardcodedSecret      scripts/management/uninstall.sh
;;   HardcodedSecret      scripts/management/backup.sh
;;   HardcodedSecret      scripts/management/init-database.sh
;;   HardcodedSecret      scripts/management/update.sh
;;   HardcodedSecret      scripts/management/health-check.sh
;;   UnboundedAllocation  cli/src/commands/feedback.rs
;;   UnboundedAllocation  cli/src/commands/sync.rs
;;   UnboundedAllocation  cli/src/config.rs
(praxis-deed
  :schema-version "1.0.0"
  :canonical-name "academic-workflow-suite-assail-classifications"
  :beholding-chora #uuid"0889b37b-defb-831f-973c-e119500db00e"
  :profile assail-classifications)
